-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261125.1~sparky9~0 (2026-11-25)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Milestone 2 (ORDER 63 and 720): one first-run window. Sparky Welcome's first-run start is skipped where the Welcome
    Center carries the edition's first page (a drop-in for app-sparky\x2dwelcome\x2dfirst@autostart.service, owned by
    this package); Sparky Welcome stays installed and in the menu as Welcome
  * After KDE's own pages: Touch and Tablet Mode; Welcome to the Sparky World!, every element of Sparky Welcome with its
    own address or command (Upgrade through sparky-stereo-welcome-upgrade, which installs the languages at its first use
    and leaves Sparky Welcome's mark, as Sparky Welcome does); Help Test Sparky Stereo OS (what the screens can do,
    copied; the edition's tracker). A program that is missing or fails is said on the page
  * The touch page can be shown only where the hardware layer finds a touch screen of the computer's own: a session
    script sets plasma-welcomerc [Distribution] TouchScreen through a folder in front of XDG_CONFIG_DIRS, read with
    Welcome.Distro.flag() (plasma-welcome 6.7.4-1+stereo3d2)
  * The first page's picture is in the page again: stereo-layer 1.23.4 shows a pair under a clip that holds it
  * The pages' words in the ten languages of the edition (domain sparky-stereo-welcome)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 20261125~sparky9~0 (2026-11-25)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Initial release (ORDER 63 and 720, milestone 1): the edition's first run is KDE's own Welcome Center (Plasma
    Welcome), which opens by itself at the first login of a new account (its kded module, LastSeenVersion empty) and not
    again after it
  * Two pages shown first, before KDE's own pages (Plasma Welcome's first-pages folder, plasma-welcome
    6.7.4-1+stereo3d1): Sparky Stereo OS in one screen, with the SparkyOS artwork's four 3D screens as a stereo pair
    (stereo-layer's StereoPicture) and a button that opens Display Configuration; and Point, Then Type, which says that the
    window under the pointer gets the keys, why (Daniel Ramos's words) and where to change it, with a button that opens
    Window Behavior and a drawing of two windows with depth on a 3D screen (stereo-layer's StereoDepth)
  * Breaks sparky-stereo-info (<< 20261125~sparky9~0), whose earlier versions kept the Welcome Center from opening at
    the first login
  * English only in this version; the ten required languages come with the remaining pages
